Ways to lose concentration:

1. Drop it voluntarily;
2. Fail a Constitution saving throw after taking damage (DC 10 or half the damage taken);
3. Have concentration on another spell (either another concentration spell or preparing a spell to cast as a reaction);
4. Being incapacitated or killed;
5. Game master's discretion because of environmental phenomena (DC 10)

Unrelated, I have a question. Why do you do

    if (pitch >= 1.1f || pitch <= 1.1f)
        pitch = 1.1f;

You will always end up setting pitch to 1.1. That condition always evaluates to true, regardless of the value of pitch: any value larger than 1.1 satisfies the first condition. Any value smaller than 1.1 satisfies the second condition. And if pitch equals 1.1, both conditions are satisfied. Since it's a logical OR connecting them, it's enough to have at least one condition satisfied.

Use tryparse instead:

    int result;
    bool parseSuccess = int.TryParse(Console.ReadLine(), out result);
